# Store/cache: ignore everything except the committed config (F28, negation fixed by F38)
# and the journal fragment carrier (issue #405, S15 — the fragments are committed
# journal entries, not store output).
# Last matching pattern wins: `/*` ignores all entries, then `!index.json`
# re-includes the committed config, `!.gitignore` re-includes this rule
# file itself, `!journal/` re-includes the opted-in fragment carrier, and
# `!journal.md` re-includes the carrier's contract document — which lives
# BESIDE the carrier, never inside it (the aggregator refuses any file there
# that is not a fragment).
# The store subdirectories (index/, custom/) and the files inside
# them stay ignored — D12 constrains store.path to this dir.
/*
!index.json
!.gitignore
!journal/
!journal.md
